    {
      "id": "3b6efafecf2c8dfb95b30d8b80897c321deb2aa8",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 511999233,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The idea looks promising but the offset is missing for sure. I would prefer to test that code with some traces first.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cccf2084a0438673e9e09f07ed0a5035f6e8815d3d5d888db0023a757c8dce8c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/LarsVoelker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-02-18T12:17:41.949Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-02-18T12:17:41.949Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 89012733,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2156,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 512300265,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I am not sure that this code has a real benefit but maybe that's because I do not see the benefit for the heuristics in automotive use cases anyhow. In automotive use cases you usually have the configuration. :)\n\nAnyhow, for the traces I looked at, this did not make a difference. But I guess you could construct a packet that would make a difference.\n\nIn order to not break it for other packets, I propose to change the function like this:\n\n```\nstatic gboolean\ntest_someip(packet_info *pinfo _U_, tvbuff_t *tvb, int offset, void *data _U_)\n{\n\n    if (tvb_captured_length_remaining(tvb, offset) < SOMEIP_HDR_LEN) {\n        return FALSE;\n    }\n\n    guint32 length = tvb_get_guint32(tvb, offset + 4, ENC_BIG_ENDIAN);\n    if (length < 8) {\n        return FALSE;\n    }\n\n    if ((tvb_get_guint8(tvb, offset + 12)) != SOMEIP_PROTOCOL_VERSION) {\n        return FALSE;\n    }\n\n    if (!try_val_to_str((tvb_get_guint8(tvb, offset + 14) & ~SOMEIP_MSGTYPE_TP_MASK), someip_msg_type)) {\n        return FALSE;\n    }\n\n    /* Assume no fragments for UDP */\n    if (pinfo->ptype == PT_UDP && tvb_captured_length_remaining(tvb, offset + 8) < (gint)length) {\n        return FALSE;\n    }\n\n    return TRUE;\n}\n```\n\nBut always, I am never 100% sure, if its tvb_captured_length_remaining or tvb_reported_length_remaining...",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cccf2084a0438673e9e09f07ed0a5035f6e8815d3d5d888db0023a757c8dce8c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/LarsVoelker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-02-18T18:12:18.896Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-02-19T00:00:28.350Z",
